b='''For the algebraic comparison, on each arithmetic component of Sh_U(3)(G,X) use its natural integral lattice local system and Hodge structures. Its arithmetic stabilizer preserves this lattice and its marking modulo3. The polarization multiplier of a rational stabilizer element is positive and a unit at every finite prime, hence equals1; therefore the polarization is integral and flat on that component. Final Milne14.8 supplies the abelian scheme algebraically. Its O-action descends by the full faithfulness in that theorem. The marking is a flat section of the finite etale isomorphism sheaf; such a section over a complex algebraic variety is algebraic, since its graph is a connected-component union in a finite etale cover. Thus the fine functor gives an algebraic comparison map from each component to Y_C. The point classification from7.4 and the integral-lattice equivalence make it bijective on geometric points. A bijective nonconstant morphism of nonsingular complex curves is an isomorphism: the function-field extension has degree1 in characteristic zero, and the local discrete valuation rings of the nonsingular curves agree. This establishes the comparison as algebraic, not merely a set bijection. All components are used, and the map commutes with forgetting level.'''
